e polling rather than the stronger fundamentals number.", "watch": "A late shift toward Rogers on the Muslim Brotherhood storyline, or turnout divergence in the Detroit suburbs versus rural Michigan, could move this into tossup territory.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Open seat: Gary Peters (D) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Michigan's open Senate seat pits Democrat Abdul El-Sayed against Republican Mike Rogers to succeed retiring Senator Gary Peters. Polling throughout October has shown a narrow but consistent Democratic edge, with recent surveys from Marist and YouGov putting El-Sayed up two to five points. Expert raters mostly call the race Lean or Tilt Democratic, though several still rate it a tossup, and prediction markets price El-Sayed around 70%.\n\nThe race remains genuinely competitive. Rogers benefits from heavy outside spending on his side and attacks questioning El-Sayed's trustworthiness, while El-Sayed has outraised Rogers and holds a modest cash edge. Michigan's near-even partisan lean keeps the ceiling low for either candidate, and the final debates have been combative and closely watched.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.7769, "margin": 3.59}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.7646, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.7534, "margin": 3.2}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.7553, "margin": 3.4}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.6955, "margin": 3.2}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.7118, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.7565, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.7778, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.755, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.7606, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.7617, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.7781, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.7877, "margin": 3.7}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.7047, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.7427, "margin": 4.0}, {"date